<title>RUSSIA: RUSSIA'S GROSS GRAIN CROP 20.0 MLN T BY AUG 4.</title>
<headline>RUSSIA'S GROSS GRAIN CROP 20.0 MLN T BY AUG 4.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's grain harvest totalled 20.0 million tonnes bunker weight as at August 4, a drop of 11.9 percent on year-ago levels, official figures showed on Friday.</p>
<p>The State Statistics Committee released the following data, its first report on the progress of the harvest:</p>
<p>	     PROGRESS IN RUSSIAN GRAIN HARVEST AS OF AUG 8</p>
<p> GRAINS, NOT INCL MAIZE:	    1997     1996     1995</p>
<p>Threshed (million tonnes,</p>
<p>	     bunker weight)	   20.0     22.7     27.7</p>
<p>  Cut (million hectares)	    10.2     14.1     20.1</p>
<p>  Cut (as pct of sown area)	 21.4     29.2     41.7</p>
<p>  Threshed (million hectares)	8.6     12.5     18.6</p>
<p>  Threshed (as pct of sown area)  17.9     26.1     38.7</p>
<p>  Threshed (as pct of cut area)   83.9     89.1     92.9</p>
<p>  Yields per hectare (tonnes)     2.34     1.81     1.48</p>
<p>It said over 70 percent of grain crops in the Northern Caucasus, which accounts for up to 40 percent of Russia's free-market grain supplies at the end of the harvest, had been cut.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
